# Secrets and machine-local state
.env

# Everything the diary writes: photographs of the page, recordings of the
# room, the store, the speech model, the cross-compiled agent, tablet
# snapshots, pidfiles and logs. All of it is either private, enormous or
# regenerable, and deleting the whole directory is a legitimate fix.
var/

# Build output and local tooling
.venv/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# The page you speak into: deps and build output. bun.lock is committed.
apps/web/node_modules/
apps/web/dist/
apps/web/.vite/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# --- old locations, kept on purpose -------------------------------------
# These moved under var/ in the reorganisation. The rules stay because a
# working tree from before it -- or a snapshot restored by hand -- can still
# put them back, and backup/rm2-* holds the tablet's private ssh keys, its
# shell history and every notebook on it. A single `git add -A` with these
# rules missing would publish all of that.
# Unanchored on purpose: a device snapshot must stay ignored wherever it
# lands, including a directory that was itself moved.
**/rm2-2*/
**/inventory-2*/
backup/rm2-*/
backup/inventory-*/
captures/
audio/
models/
riddle.db*
memories.txt
.riddle_session
.riddle.pid
.voice.pid
riddle.log
voice.log
bin/
web/node_modules/
web/dist/
web/.vite/
*.zip
*.tar
*.tar.gz
